====================================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  DONE PROPERLY, ITEM 71 COLLAPSES, and this script retracts the previous one.  Three things are true and they do not add up to a test:
  (i) the negative-mass region at the saddle is real (h71_saddle_point.py) and is a few kpc across;
  (ii) the control is PROVEN, not argued -- two NFW halos give exactly the sum of their parts, because Newtonian gravity is linear,
       so a genuine pair-versus-sum difference could not be manufactured by any arrangement of dark matter;
  (iii) but there is essentially no difference to measure.  Centred where a survey can actually centre -- on a galaxy, in Delta Sigma
       -- the pair-versus-sum ratio is 1.000 to 1.023 across 50-180 kpc, a 0-2% effect sitting on a signal three orders of magnitude
       larger, and of the wrong SIGN (a small excess, not a deficit).
  The previous script's 67% deficit came from centring on the saddle and using Sigma instead of Delta Sigma; the saddle is a local
  MINIMUM, so that statistic is dominated by where the aperture sits rather than by the gravity law.  ITEM 71 IS DEMOTED, its earlier
  promotion is WITHDRAWN, and the honest summary is: a beautiful sign-definite signature of nonlinear gravity that the observable
  washes out.

